  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LRCs Conflict Preparedness and Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1- Preparedness: 
Set up a Preparedness plan under the following areas: EMS, BTS, MSS, DMS, and Youth. 
2- Response:
I. Response in Affected Areas: Triage &amp; first aid, Hospital coordination, Patient transportation, Dead Body management, Interfacility transport, Evacuations, Relief distribution. 
II. Response to Internal Displacement in Receiving Areas: Provision of EMS services, Collection and provision of Blood units by BTS, Provision of primary heath services, Initial needs assessments, Acute shelter, WASH, Ecosec and RFL services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LRC&apos;s Crisis Management Plan underscores the national society&#x2019;s commitment to delivering timely and effective assistance to those affected by the conflict. Through the coordinated efforts of its various sectors, LRC will prioritize saving lives, alleviating suffering, and providing essential services to both those in affected areas and those who have been internally displaced, in line with its humanitarian mission and principles.</narrative>
  </description>
